Read AGENTS.md and the canonical GitHub issue via gh. The full JSON assignment below supplies run_id, repository, issue_url, project_id, workspace, branch, baseline, evidence_dir and acceptance. Verify pwd, origin remote, branch and base ancestry before work. Use only the assigned worktree. GitHub Issues are authoritative; no BB Tasks records. Keep the issue open. Harness owns GitHub comments, PR publication and completion assertions. Graph routing owns dispatch. Do not spawn other workers. Evidence files go in evidence_dir. Authorized git commits can require exec_command sandbox_permissions=require_escalated because shared Git metadata is read-only. Request that escalation with the concrete reason if needed. On rejection return BLOCKED with the stated reason.
Assignment: {{input}}
Implement the tiny acceptance change in greeting.py and test_greeting.py only. Run python3 -m unittest -v, commit with the full issue URL in the message, then run python3 tools/validate.py --evidence EVIDENCE_DIR --role implementor --run-id RUN_ID substituting the assignment values. Verify the checkout is clean. READY FOR REVIEW requires two passing tests, a full committed candidate_sha, and the validation record. Return one JSON object containing all declared result fields as your final response. validation_evidence is a native list field: return an array containing the absolute implementor.json path. On revisits address reviewer findings.
Latest review: {{reviewer}}
TEST-ONLY LIVE FAULT INJECTION, explicitly authorized by the review-revision assignment. This run deliberately creates a review defect while keeping two tests green. Before the FIRST implementation commit run python3 -m smoke.fault_injection seed ASSIGNMENT_FILE with cwd=HARNESS_ROOT (values in assignment), then implement normal acceptance while retaining the injected comment in greeting.py. After validate.py copy implementor.json to implementor-initial.json in evidence_dir. Do not remove the comment during the first pass. On the revisit, Latest review must contain smoke-revision-feedback:RUN_ID and the rejected SHA. Run python3 -m smoke.fault_injection revise ASSIGNMENT_FILE with cwd=HARNESS_ROOT to remove it and record feedback-receipt.json; commit the correction as a NEW commit, validate again and return the NEW SHA. Include the received feedback token in notes. No new issue, branch or PR. All fault injection and validation run on the assigned worktree only.

