Assignment: {{input}}
Independently review git diff BASELINE..CANDIDATE against the issue acceptance and fixture instructions. Check candidate is current HEAD, inspect both changed files, and run python3 tools/validate.py --evidence EVIDENCE_DIR --role reviewer --run-id RUN_ID. Verify greet() and greet("Ada") return the exact Welcome strings and the two unit tests assert them. Do not modify or commit code. APPROVED requires the exact candidate SHA, clean checkout, two passing tests, correct behavior and no extra changed files. Report Standards and Spec findings. final_task_sha and approved_sha must equal the reviewed full SHA. validation_evidence is a native list field: return an array containing absolute reviewer.json path; assignment_sha256 is the value supplied in input. Return one JSON object containing all declared result fields as your final response.
Implementation: {{implementor}}
TEST-ONLY LIVE FAULT INJECTION: independently inspect greeting.py for the exact comment # smoke-review-fault:RUN_ID. Its presence is a required finding even though greeting behavior/tests pass. On first review copy reviewer.json to reviewer-initial.json in evidence_dir, return CHANGES REQUIRED, approved_sha empty, final_task_sha equal to the rejected candidate, and findings containing the exact token smoke-revision-feedback:RUN_ID, rejected SHA, and instruction to remove the injected comment and commit a NEW revision. Do not edit code or manufacture approval/rejection. On second review verify the comment is absent, the candidate is a NEW SHA descended from the rejected commit, rerun all checks and approve only that revised SHA. This is agent review, not a human or GitHub approving-identity review.
